          "number": 5,
          "letter": "E",
          "english": "\"I diagnose them through conversation,\" says Dr. Mustahid. \"Sometimes it's really obvious things that local doctors don't have the patience to talk through with their patients. For example, a common complaint mothers come in with is that their children refuse to eat their meals. The mothers are concerned they are dealing with indigestion, but it's because they are feeding the children packaged chips which are cheap and convenient. I tell them it is ruining their appetite and ask them to cut back on unhealthy snacks.\" Dr. Mustahid says building awareness about health and nutrition is important for island patients who are cut off from mainland resources.",
          "chinese": "穆斯塔希德医生说：“我是通过交谈来诊断他们的。有时，事情其实非常明显，只是当地医生没有耐心和患者仔细沟通。例如，母亲们来就诊时常见的一个抱怨是，她们的孩子拒绝吃饭。母亲们担心孩子消化不良，但实际上是因为她们给孩子吃了包装薯片，这种食物既便宜又方便。我告诉她们，这会破坏孩子的食欲，并让她们减少不健康零食的摄入。”穆斯塔希德医生说，对于与大陆资源隔绝的岛上患者而言，提高健康和营养意识十分重要。",
