          "number": 7,
          "letter": "G",
          "english": "For most TD patients on the islands, Dr. Mustahid is the first big-city doctor that they've ever consulted. TD doctors are not meant to treat serious illnesses or conditions that require a doctor to be physically present, such as pregnancy. But they can write prescriptions, diagnose common ailments—including digestive issues, joint pain, skin diseases, fever and the common cold—and refer patients to doctors at local hospitals. The visit is also an opportunity for the patients, especially women, to air their concerns about aging, motherhood and reproductive health according to Dr. Mustahid. The doctors also offer health, dietary and lifestyle advice where necessary, including insight on everything from recognizing postnatal(产后的) depression to daily exercise. Dr. Mustahid regularly recommends her patients to take a daily thirty-minute morning walk before the sun gets too intense.",
          "chinese": "对于岛上大多数TD患者来说，穆斯塔希德医生是她们一生中咨询过的第一位大城市医生。TD的医生并不负责治疗重病，也不负责处理需要医生亲自到场的情况，例如妊娠。但他们可以开具处方，诊断常见疾病，包括消化问题、关节疼痛、皮肤病、发烧和普通感冒，并将患者转诊给当地医院的医生。穆斯塔希德医生说，就诊也是患者，尤其是女性，倾诉自己对衰老、母亲身份和生殖健康方面担忧的机会。必要时，医生还会提供健康、饮食和生活方式方面的建议，内容包括如何识别产后抑郁以及进行日常锻炼等各个方面。穆斯塔希德医生经常建议患者每天早晨步行30分钟，时间要赶在太阳变得过于强烈之前。",
